WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
What do I remember about it.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.820
About Old Spanish Trail.

3
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.280
I do know that as a kid growing up, you know,

4
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:15.000
we heard a lot of stories about the gold being found along the Old Spanish Trail.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
That’s a very prevalent thing in this area.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:32.600
John . . . Jean Lafitte was the pirate that was in this area that the Contraband Days [Louisiana Pirate Festival that takes place in Lake Charles] is named after.

7
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.920
So there are lots and lots of stories about gold.

8
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:44.820
In fact, to the extent that when I was a very young kid, I don’t recall it personally,

9
00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:54.800
but I was told about . . . My father got up early one morning before day to go to work and he heard noise outside.

10
00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:07.220
It was a lady that was a schoolteacher was outside digging up the yard because she somehow had determined that there was treasures buried at a certain point.

11
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:14.060
He caught her out here digging the yard up, trying to find the treasure.

12
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:27.500
Those stories are very prevalent along the Old Spanish Trail, and some areas off . . . other streets that parallel that area.

13
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.560
My high school was on the Old Spanish Trail.

14
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.220
The swimming pool was on the Old Spanish Trail.

15
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:54.140
Essentially all the things that were special to the area: a little burger stand, grocery store, church, all along the Old Spanish Trail on that street.

16
00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.120
We played in that street, I mean, quite a bit.

17
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:09.440
It wasn’t a major highway, so we played alongside the road, rode our bicycles along the side.

18
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:16.040
It was a path to go anywhere that we were going in our area was just following the Old Spanish Trail.
